1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Jordan Blake: Marcus, good to meet you. Thanks for taking the time.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Marcus Reyes: Yeah, no problem. I've got about twenty minutes before a service call.

3
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:16,000
Jordan Blake: Perfect, I'll keep it tight. What's the main thing you want to fix in how Harbor Line gets customers?

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:30,000
Marcus Reyes: The leads we get are mostly tire kickers. People who want a free quote on a new system and then go with the cheapest guy, or people who just want to know what a tune-up costs and never book.

5
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,000
Jordan Blake: Where are those leads coming from today?

6
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:48,000
Marcus Reyes: Google Ads mostly. My nephew set it up and he runs it on the side. We spend about two thousand a month and I honestly think most of it is wasted. I can't tell you what we get for it.

7
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:53,000
Jordan Blake: How many installs did those ads bring in last month?

8
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:02,000
Marcus Reyes: Maybe two installs. Average install for us is around nine thousand. Service calls are more like three hundred.

9
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:08,000
Jordan Blake: And is demand steady through the year, or does it swing?

10
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:20,000
Marcus Reyes: It's feast or famine. July and January we can't keep up. April and October the phone barely rings and I'm still paying six techs.

11
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:28,000
Jordan Blake: So in the slow months, what would it take to keep those six techs busy?

12
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:36,000
Marcus Reyes: Probably eight more installs a month in the shoulder seasons, plus maintenance plans.

13
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:52,000
Jordan Blake: Okay. You mentioned the leads are tire kickers and the ad spend feels wasted. So here's what we'd change. We qualify every lead before it hits your calendar, with questions on system age, budget and timeline, and we push maintenance plan offers in April and October when you said the phone goes quiet.

14
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:58,000
Marcus Reyes: That sounds good on paper. What's the price?

15
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:04,000
Jordan Blake: Two thousand setup, two thousand eight hundred a month, plus the ad budget you're already spending.

16
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:12,000
Marcus Reyes: Man, that's expensive. That's more than I pay my nephew by a lot.

17
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:24,000
Jordan Blake: It is more. Let me ask, what does your nephew report to you each month? Cost per booked install, close rate, anything like that?

18
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:30,000
Marcus Reyes: Not really. He sends me a screenshot with clicks.

19
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:44,000
Jordan Blake: So right now two thousand a month goes out and you can't see what comes back. You told me an install is nine thousand. If we add two installs a month, the fee is covered and you know exactly which dollars did it.

20
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:54,000
Marcus Reyes: Can you guarantee that? Like if you don't get me the installs I don't pay?

21
00:02:54,500 --> 00:03:12,000
Jordan Blake: I won't guarantee installs, because I don't control your techs or your pricing. What I guarantee is the process: campaigns live in ten days, every lead called within five minutes, and a weekly report on cost per booked appointment. And we do a ninety day first term, not a year, so you can judge us on real numbers.

22
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:18,000
Marcus Reyes: Ninety days I could live with. Ninety days is fair.

23
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:26,000
Marcus Reyes: Let me think about it over the weekend though. I want to look at the numbers.

24
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:34,000
Jordan Blake: Of course. What specifically do you want to run the numbers on? Maybe we can do it together now.

25
00:03:34,500 --> 00:03:44,000
Marcus Reyes: Mostly whether I can carry the fee in April before it starts paying off. Cash gets tight in the spring.

26
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:56,000
Jordan Blake: That's fair. We can split the setup across the first two months so April isn't heavy. Are you ready to move forward if the setup is split like that?

27
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:04,000
Marcus Reyes: Yeah, if the setup is split I'm in. Send the agreement and let's get started.

28
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:12,000
Jordan Blake: Great. I'll send the agreement today and book the kickoff for Monday at ten. Does that work?

29
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:16,000
Marcus Reyes: Monday at ten works.
